 5198 A:e271                                    ;
 5199 A:e271                                    ; "STRLT2" TAKES THE STRING LITERAL WHOSE FIRST CHARACTER
 5200 A:e271                                    ; IS POINTED TO BY [Y,A] AND BUILDS A DESCRIPTOR FOR IT.
 5201 A:e271                                    ; THE DESCRIPTOR IS INITIALLY BUILT IN "DSCTMP", BUT "PUTNEW"
 5202 A:e271                                    ; TRANSFERS IT INTO A TEMPORARY AND LEAVES A POINTER
 5203 A:e271                                    ; AT THE TEMPORARY IN FACMO&LO. THE CHARACTERS OTHER THAN
 5204 A:e271                                    ; ZERO THAT TERMINATE THE STRING SHOULD BE SET UP IN "CHARAC"
 5205 A:e271                                    ; AND "ENDCHR". IF THE TERMINATOR IS A QUOTE, THE QUOTE IS SKIPPED
 5206 A:e271                                    ; OVER. LEADING QUOTES SHOULD BE SKIPPED BEFORE JSR. ON RETURN
 5207 A:e271                                    ; THE CHARACTER AFTER THE STRING LITERAL IS POINTED TO
 5208 A:e271                                    ; BY [STRNG2].
 5209 A:e271                                    ;
